shape theory.character : theory.shape {
  type: definition
  layer: 0
  """
// Definition 3.2 (Character).
// The character of a shape, denoted C, is the aspect that changes:
// the specific configuration at a given point, the particular state
// right now.
//
// Character is what distinguishes one state from another state of
// the same shape. Two shapes with identical structure may differ in
// character: traversing different sequences of states.
//
// Structure corresponds to continuity. Character corresponds to change.
// The axiom requires both; the shape has both.
//
// Crucially, character is itself persistence structure. The values
// character takes (positions, angles, configurations) are themselves
// structural. Everything is persistence structure at every level of
// the fractal. The distinction between S and C is a distinction of
// role at a given level, not two ontological categories.
//
// Derives from: theory.shape (the axiom forces the S/C decomposition)
  """
}
